    "body": "## Summary\n\nRevert ADR-079. Original fix caused production Wikipedia regression:\n\n- Body text and infobox overlap (block full width, no line-wrap, text runs into float territory)\n- Header broken (huge logo, hamburger overlapping)\n- 10x layout slowdown (PERF-LAYOUT 2000ms -> 20000ms after wiring fix)\n\n## Three bugs identified\n\n**Bug A (pre-existing, blocking):** `clear: right` on a float advances cursor_y for siblings. Sidebar's clear pushes cursor_y past infobox bottom (1545.5), so intro paragraphs start at y=1553 (below float), not y≈750 (beside it). No line-wrap can fire.\n\n**Bug B (wired, exposed C):** `parent_float_ctx` not consumed in `make_inline_float_ctx`. Wire fix correct but exposed C.\n\n**Bug C (10x perf):** `start_y_absolute` passed to breaker is `cursor_y` (relative), but `float_ctx.bottom` is absolute. Comparing local y=0 vs absolute 1545 → every descendant thinks it should wrap → explosion.\n\n## Path forward\n\nPreserved on branch `wip/adr-079-line-wrap` (DO NOT MERGE — WIP reference only). Trace logs at /tmp/adr-079-preserved/.\n\nNext session:\n1. Fix Bug A (clear:cursor_y advance)\n2. Fix Bug C (absolute y threading)\n3. Re-wire Bug B (copy from WIP branch)\n4. **Verify on Wikipedia BEFORE merging** — fixture tests passed twice while production broke. ADR-070 lesson repeated.\n\nRefs #287",
    "closed_at": "2026-11-16T09:50:56Z",
